Beanjar's test guest userland, as built by beanjar-vendor (testguest/)

Everything in rootfs.squashfs and sysroot/ is built by Buildroot from upstream releases, with the
toolchain Buildroot builds itself; nothing in it is Beanjar's own code. Each part keeps its
own licence:

- BusyBox: GPL-2.0 (archival/libarchive/bz: bzip2-1.0.4)
- Mesa (EGL, OpenGL ES, GBM, the virgl gallium driver): MIT, SGI-B-2.0, Khronos
- libdrm, libpthread-stubs, expat: MIT
- zlib: Zlib
- the GNU C Library, libgcc and libstdc++, from Buildroot's own toolchain: LGPL-2.1-or-later (the
  C library) and GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception (the GCC runtime
  libraries)
- Buildroot's skeleton and init scripts: GPL-2.0-or-later

manifest.csv lists every package with its version, licence and source; licenses/ holds their
licence texts, and buildroot.config the configuration they were built with. The sources of the
packages, with the patches Buildroot applied, and Buildroot's own release are in the release's
testguest-<version>-legal-info.tar, the toolchain's (GCC, glibc, the Linux headers) among them.
